# Build artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
/.site/
/site/

# Bare `go build ./cmd/...` binaries dropped at the repo root. The Makefile
# builds into dist/; these are stray local builds and must never be committed.
/trstctl
/trstctl-agent
/trstctl-cli
/trstctl-signer

# Web UI dependencies are never committed.
/web/node_modules/
/web/coverage/

# Keep Java SDK sources trackable even if a local exclude pattern overmatches
# the com/trstctl package path.
!clients/sdk/java/src/
!clients/sdk/java/src/**

# Keep shipped-binary DoD tests trackable when a developer-local exclude uses
# the broad package-name pattern `trstctl` (which also matches cmd/trstctl/).
!cmd/trstctl/
!cmd/trstctl/dod_pqc_runtime_test.go
!cmd/trstctl/dod_kmip_runtime_test.go

# The built web console under internal/webui/dist IS committed (EXC-WIRE-04 /
# SURFACE-001): it is the artifact the Go binary embeds via //go:embed, so a plain
# `go build ./cmd/trstctl` (no `make web` step) serves the REAL React console, not a
# dead placeholder. Regenerate it with `make web` (CI re-runs this and the
# TRSTCTL_REQUIRE_BUILT_UI release gate so the committed bundle cannot drift to the
# placeholder). Do NOT ignore it.

# Supply-chain scan cache. scripts/supply-chain/verify-embedded-postgres.sh
# extracts the ~2.5G embedded-postgres runtime into /.supply-chain for
# checksum-pinning and Trivy scanning; it is a local cache and must never be
# committed (it is also excluded from the Docker build context in .dockerignore).
/.supply-chain/

# Test and coverage output
*.out
*.test
coverage.*
cover.out.*
/coverage/
# Python substrate-test bytecode is local interpreter output, never source.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Volatile DoD receipt: make dod-gate always emits a fresh timestamped census.
/wiring-census.json

# Go workspace files (not committed; per-developer)
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Local mount cruft & non-source artifacts (added 2026-07-05) ---
# FUSE mount orphan files (created when an open file is deleted on the mount)
.fuse_hidden*
# Node deps for non-web SDKs (mirrors /web/node_modules; never committed)
**/node_modules/
# Local dev cert served by the test harness; never commit key/cert material
served-ca.pem
# Go build temp files, e.g. trstctl-agent.exe-go-tmp-umask
*-go-tmp-umask
# Non-standard coverage output that escapes the *.out rule
cover.out.nogen
# Local scratch/build markers
.__b__
.__scratch_test__
.__target__

# Internal working docs (audits, sprint plans, decision records) are local
# working artifacts, not committable repo content.
docs-internal/

# S-C4/S-C8: browser-test and workbench artifacts (baselines under
# web/e2e/**-snapshots ARE committed; reports and builds are not)
/web/test-results/
/web/playwright-report/
/web/.storybook-static/

# AH-0002: AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md are agent-tooling working files, not product
# documentation, and this repository ships publicly. The canonical contract lives
# outside the repo (../agents-contract/). Bare patterns so they match at every
# depth. docs/agent_contract_files_test.go (CODE-105) is the load-bearing gate —
# .gitignore is advisory and `git add -f` walks straight past it.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Agent/editor session state. .claude/ holds per-machine Claude Code settings and
# hooks. It was previously excluded only via .git/info/exclude, which is local to
# one checkout and is never published - so a fresh clone showed it as untracked
# AND unignored, and the first `git add -A` in that clone would stage it (AH-0ffc461f).
.claude/
